# Project conventions

This repo ingests Australian higher-education public data into a DuckDB warehouse,
serves it via FastAPI, and renders it in a Next.js dashboard. See `AGENTS.md` for
the full guide.

## Architecture boundaries

- Parsers (`src/uni_intel/ingestion/parsers/`) are pure: file bytes to dataclass
  rows. No network, no DB, no side effects.
- Runners (`src/uni_intel/ingestion/ingest_*.py`) own I/O: download, stage,
  resolve providers, load facts, write quality checks.
- Shared ETL helpers live in `src/uni_intel/ingestion/common.py`. Do not fork
  private copies of checksum/id/upsert/quality logic into individual runners.
- The API is layered: `api/app.py` (factory) -> `api/routers/*` (HTTP) ->
  `api/repositories/*` (SQL) -> `api/analytics.py` (pure math). Keep SQL out of
  routers and keep routers thin.

## Data access

- Always go through `src/uni_intel/db.py` for DuckDB connections; use its context
  manager rather than calling `duckdb.connect` directly.
- Use parameterized SQL (`?` placeholders). Never interpolate query/user values
  into SQL strings.
- The API opens connections read-only.

## Style

- Keep modules focused and under ~400 lines; split when they grow past that.
- Public functions get type hints. New API responses get Pydantic models.
- Do not change the public HTTP API contract without updating the API tests.
- Regenerate/refresh the warehouse archive only via `make ingest-all` +
  `make archive-db`; do not hand-edit `data/warehouse/*`.
